WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:07.197
NIST SP 800-63-4 measures
digital identity on three scales:

2
00:00:07.197 --> 00:00:10.538
identity proofing,
authentication, and federation.

3
00:00:10.538 --> 00:00:14.334
For a partner person, the partner
usually performs the first two,

4
00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:18.274
and the agency decides whether
that's enough for each transaction.

5
00:00:18.274 --> 00:00:20.647
The levels come from an impact assessment,

6
00:00:20.647 --> 00:00:23.425
and partner persons are
their own user group in it.

7
00:00:23.425 --> 00:00:28.197
A bank officer submitting a financial
filing and a state examiner reading a case

8
00:00:28.197 --> 00:00:31.474
summary can land at different
levels on the same system,

9
00:00:31.474 --> 00:00:36.175
so the record holds one row per protected
transaction, not one level per partner.

10
00:00:36.175 --> 00:00:37.987
Two federal rules shape this.

11
00:00:37.987 --> 00:00:44.421
M-22-09 requires phishing-resistant MFA
for agency staff, contractors and partners,

12
00:00:44.421 --> 00:00:48.041
but leaves each agency to
define the partner category,

13
00:00:48.041 --> 00:00:51.499
so the agency writes its
definition into the record.

14
00:00:51.499 --> 00:00:56.795
And FIPS 201-3 covers federal employees
and contractors only, so never call a

15
00:00:56.795 --> 00:01:01.630
partner credential PIV-equivalent unless
a policy the agency can cite says so.
